#     OPTIONS, PAUSE OPTIONS, NUMBER PROCESSING OPTIONS, SUBSTITUTION
#     OPTIONS, PRESENTATION OPTIONS.
# - While reorganizing, found (via an automated completeness check
#     comparing every CLI flag against the new help text) two more
#     flags that had never been documented at all, even before this
#     reorganization: -manner/-man and -place/-pl. Added them, alongside
#     the -phon/-voicing/-phonword entries added in v1.9.111, since
#     they're the same category (direct-switch equivalents of
#     --format=MANNER and --format=PLACE).
# - Verified: all 77 CLI flags are now documented in -h (zero gaps),
#     confirmed via the same automated check.
#
# v1.9.111
# - Added -h help-text documentation (both English and Spanish) for every
#     flag identified as undocumented in the previous audit: the whole CH
#     SHORTCUTS family (-chsc, -chrl, -chrnl, -chnrl, -chnrnl), -phon/-fon/
#     -ph (direct switch, equivalent to --format=PH), -voicing/-voice/-v
#     (direct switch, equivalent to --format=V), -phonword/-pw, -times/
#     -times-colon/-twc, and -split-syls/-div-sil/-sas/-des. No functional
#     changes -- these flags already worked, they just weren't documented.
#
# v1.9.110
# - Documentation audit: checked every CLI flag against the -h help text,
#     and every perkins.ini-whitelisted variable against perkins.ini itself.
# - Found and fixed a real gap from the MFA->MFA rename: perkins.ini still
#     had an entry for the old "mfa_format" variable name, which no longer
#     exists -- uncommenting it would have been silently rejected as an
#     unknown variable. Renamed to "mfa_format" and corrected the
#     description (it used to say tildes are stripped from the
#     orthographic column; that's no longer true since the MFA
#     tilde-preservation fix).
# - Added a help-text entry for -tvd (triple_vowels_to_double), which had
#     never been documented at all, even under its old name (-dvs).
# - Noted, but left as-is (pre-existing, not something this project
#     introduced): -split-syls, the whole CH SHORTCUTS family (-chsc,
#     -chrl, -chrnl, -chnrl, -chnrnl), -phon, -phonword, -times, and
#     -voicing have no dedicated help-text entries either. Flagged for
#     awareness; not fixed here since they predate all our changes.
#
# v1.9.109
# - Corrected where the IPA stress mark attaches in MFA mode: it now
#     skips past any onset consonant(s) and attaches specifically to the
#     VOWEL of the stressed syllable, e.g. "chile" -> "tʃ ˈi l e" (not
#     "ˈtʃ i l e"), "america" -> "a m ˈe ɾ i k a" (not "a ˈm e ɾ i k a"),
#     and "posee" -> "p o s ˈe e" (not "p o ˈs e e"). The v1.9.107 fix
#     had attached the mark to whichever phoneme came right after it
#     (consonant or vowel), which happened to look right for onset-only
#     stressed syllables but was wrong whenever a consonant intervened.
#
# v1.9.108
# - Renamed $double_vowels_to_singles to $triple_vowels_to_double
#     throughout (CLI flag --dvs -> --tvd, function
#     double_vowels_to_single_vowels -> triple_vowels_to_double_vowels,
#     settings-table label, perkins.ini entry, and comments), and changed
#     its behavior: a run of THREE OR MORE identical vowels now collapses
#     to TWO (not one), e.g. "nooo" -> "noo", "siii" -> "sii". A run of
#     exactly two is left untouched -- this fixes real Spanish double
#     vowels (e.g. "leer", "creer") that were previously, incorrectly,
#     being collapsed to a single vowel.
# - Also fixed a latent bug found in the process: the call to this
#     function was never actually gated on the flag at all -- it ran
#     unconditionally regardless of --tvd/--notvd or perkins.ini. Now
#     properly wired up: --notvd genuinely disables the collapsing.
# - Regression suite: added a corpus file and two new cases specifically
#     covering this (default vs --notvd) with both 3+-vowel runs and
#     genuine double vowels in the same input.
#
# v1.9.107
# - In MFA mode, the IPA stress mark (ˈ primary, ˌ secondary) now attaches
#     directly to the phoneme immediately following it, rather than
#     appearing as its own separate space-separated token, e.g.
#     "Chile" -> "ˈtʃ i l e" and "América" -> "a ˈm e ɾ i k a" (previously
#     "ˈ tʃ i l e" / "a ˈ m e ɾ i k a"). Only affects build_mfa_phoneme_
#     string()'s tokenization when stress_using_tildes==0; --st output
#     (tilde-marked vowels) is unchanged.
#
# v1.9.106
# - Renamed the MFA output feature to MFA (Grapheme-to-Phoneme) throughout:
#     the CLI flag (--mfa -> --mfa), the internal variable ($mfa_format ->
#     $mfa_format), the function that builds the phoneme list
#     (build_mfa_phoneme_string -> build_mfa_phoneme_string), the output
#     file extension (.MFA -> .MFA), the settings-table label, help text,
#     and surrounding comments. Explanatory mentions of the actual
#     Montreal Forced Aligner tool (MFA) were kept where they provide
#     genuine context (e.g. "compatible with tools such as the Montreal
#     Forced Aligner (MFA)"), since that's a real external tool's name,
#     not the renamed feature itself. Historical changelog entries were
#     left as written, since they're a record of what the feature was
#     called at the time.
# - Fixed the orthographic (left-hand) column of MFA output to preserve
#     any tildes/accent marks that existed in the original word (e.g.
#     "área", "está", "compañía") instead of stripping them. Previously
#     they were removed along with everything else non-alphabetic;
#     now only the accent-stripping step was removed, so real letters
#     (including ñ and accented vowels) survive, while punctuation and
#     other non-letter characters are still stripped as before.
#
# v1.9.105
# - The uploaded script still had one of the two conflicting MFA-preset
#     assignments to $stress_using_tildes from the previous bug (the
#     "= 0" one -- the "= 1" one had been removed, but not this one),
#     so it was still unconditionally forced to 0 in --mfa mode
#     regardless of --st or perkins.ini. Removed it -- the MFA preset no
#     longer touches stress_using_tildes at all.
# - Separately, build_mfa_phoneme_string()'s character whitelist never
#     allowed the IPA stress marks (ˈ primary, ˌ secondary) through at
#     all, so even with stress_using_tildes correctly at 0, MFA output
#     showed no stress marking whatsoever -- identical to stress being
#     off entirely, which is what made "-mfa" and "-mfa -st" look the
#     same. Added ˈ/ˌ to the whitelist, symmetric with how accented
#     vowels are already preserved for stress_using_tildes==1. Verified
#     "-mfa" (default) now shows ˈ before the onset of the stressed
#     syllable (standard IPA placement, e.g. "estrecha" -> "e s ˈ t ɾ e
#     tʃ a"), and "-mfa -st" is unaffected and still shows the tilde-
#     marked vowel (e.g. "e s t ɾ é tʃ a") -- the two modes now produce
#     genuinely different, and each individually correct, output.
# - Regression suite: re-recorded the default --mfa golden fixtures
#     (they previously had NO stress marking baked in as "correct").
#
# v1.9.104
# - Fixed a second, deeper bug behind the vowel-dropping report: the MFA
#     preset (inside forcibly_set_variables()) contained two conflicting,
#     unconditional assignments to $stress_using_tildes within the SAME
#     block -- first "= 0", then later "= 1" -- so MFA mode always forced
#     tilde-based stress internally regardless of what the user actually
#     set via --st or perkins.ini. Combined with the previous fix (which
#     made build_mfa_phoneme_string() correctly preserve accented vowels
#     when stress_using_tildes==1), this meant EVERY --mfa run showed
#     stressed vowels with tildes, even without --st, and there was no
#     way to get plain, unstressed MFA output at all. Fixed by removing
#     both forced assignments from the MFA preset, so it no longer
#     touches stress_using_tildes -- the setting now works as expected:
#     off by default (plain vowels), on when the user explicitly enables
#     it (stressed vowels keep their tilde in the phoneme column, e.g.
#     "perro" -> "p é r o" instead of "p e r o").
# - Regression suite: re-recorded the --mfa golden fixtures (they had
#     tildes baked in as "default" output, which was itself a symptom of
#     this bug) and confirmed diverse_mfa (no --st) and diverse_mfa_st
#     (--st) now produce genuinely different, correct output.
#
# v1.9.103
# - Fixed a serious bug in build_mfa_phoneme_string(): stressed vowels
#     were silently dropped from --mfa output whenever they reached this
#     function still marked with a written accent (á é í ó ú, ü) instead
#     of an IPA stress apostrophe. This is the internal representation
#     used while stress_using_tildes==1 (--st), and it turns out some
#     stressed vowels reach this function still in that form even by
#     default -- so the bug affected plain --mfa output too, not just
#     --st combined with --mfa, e.g. "importante" -> "i m p o ɾ t n t e"
#     (missing the stressed "a"), "cinco" -> "s n k o" (missing "i").
#     Fixed by normalizing any remaining accented vowel to its plain
#     phoneme form before the character whitelist filter runs. Verified
#     against the full regression corpus: several previously-recorded
#     golden .MFA fixtures had this exact bug baked in as "expected"
#     output and had to be corrected. Added a new case combining --st
#     with --mfa specifically to guard against this regressing.
#
# v1.9.102
# - Added a new CLI option, --config-file/--cfg-file/--configfile/-cf, to
#     specify the configuration file by name instead of the hardcoded
#     "perkins.ini" (e.g. --config-file=corpora.ini or -cf hardwork.cfg).
