# - Made x the default representation of "CH"
# - Found a serious, wide-reaching pre-existing bug while checking
#     perkins.ini for missing variables: the ENTIRE perkins.ini
#     variable-loading mechanism (the $$var = $value symbolic-reference
#     assignment in the config-file reader) had been silently broken for
#     every single variable since `use strict` was added (v2.0.3) --
#     uncommenting ANY setting in perkins.ini (not just the two below)
#     would crash with "Can't use string ('debug') as a SCALAR ref while
#     'strict refs' in use". This slipped through because no existing
#     test ever exercised a live, actively-set perkins.ini -- only a
#     missing/unopenable one. Fixed by scoping `no strict 'refs'` tightly
#     around just that one assignment; the whitelist check immediately
#     above it already guarantees $var is a known-safe package variable
