     # [REMOVED: lowercase Roman numeral rule conflicts with Spanish words]
     # [REMOVED: lowercase Roman numeral rule conflicts with Spanish words]

     # SINGLE-CHAR ROMAN NUMERALS: I, V, X MUST COME AFTER MULTI-CHAR ONES
     # so that e.g. "viii" is caught before "v" could gobble its first char.
     # These are case-insensitive (/i flag) so that uppercase "I", "V", "X"
     # (as typed in running text) are handled before spell_out_single_letters
